  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「シバムギ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%82%B7%E3%83%90%E3%83%A0%E3%82%AE",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 107273802,
      "text": "シバムギ は、単子葉植物イネ科シバムギ属に属する雑草の一種。ヒメカモジグサともよばれることがある。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Elymus repens」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elymus_repens",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1366011475,
      "text": "Elymus repens, commonly known as couch grass, is a very common perennial species of grass native to most of Europe, Asia, the Arctic, and northwest Africa. It has been brought into other mild northern climates for forage or erosion control, but it often becomes invasive in the area."
    }
